d betting markets all point the same way. Bailey's cost-and-safety message and the cycle's lone debate have shown no sign of changing that trajectory.", "watch": "A late-breaking scandal or a cost-of-living backlash that surges downstate turnout could narrow the margin, though the outcome would still likely favor Pritzker.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Incumbent JB Pritzker (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Illinois' governor's race is a rematch of 2022, when incumbent JB Pritzker defeated Darren Bailey by a double-digit margin. Pritzker enters with the advantages of incumbency, a Democratic-leaning state, and vast personal resources; headlines show him spending in other states' contests, a sign of confidence at home. Bailey has campaigned on costs and public safety and met Pritzker in a single, testy debate, but has shown little evidence of expanding beyond his downstate base.\n\nEvery major race rating places Illinois in the safest Democratic category, and surveys of likely voters show Pritzker ahead by roughly twenty points. Betting markets price his reelection at about 97 percent. The forecast expects Pritzker to win comfortably, with the main uncertainty being the size of the margin rather than the outcome.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.98, "margin": 13.88}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9829, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.983, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9789, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9753, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9721, "margin": 13.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9755, "margin": 13.9}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9748, "margin": 13.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9823, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9825, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9825, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9786, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9788, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2